<item>
            <title>[LU-20918] Install modules under /usr/lib/modules on SLES 16</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20918</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;SLES 16 is usr-merged, and weak-modules2 only searches&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;/usr/lib/modules for kernel modules. Modules installed under&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;/lib/modules are not seen by it, so they are not handled when the&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;kernel package is updated.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For suse_version &amp;gt;= 1600, make lustre.spec.in use /usr/lib/modules:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;alternate&quot; type=&quot;square&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;set modules_fs_path to /usr/lib/modules/%{_kver}/%{kmoddir}&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;ul class=&quot;alternate&quot; type=&quot;square&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;after &quot;make install&quot;, move $RPM_BUILD_ROOT/lib/modules to&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&#160; $RPM_BUILD_ROOT/usr/lib/modules and remove the empty lib directory&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;alternate&quot; type=&quot;square&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;run the find-debuginfo.sh chmod step on /usr/lib/modules&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Other distributions continue to use /lib/modules.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
